<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Trent</h1><p class="st-meta">569 CE – 774 CE (approx.) · capital Trento</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lombard frontier duchy in the Adige valley guarding the Brenner route into Italy against Franks and Bavarians.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Soon after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> invasion of 568, a duchy was set up at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Tridentum</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-trent">Trento</a>) to control the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adige">Adige</a> valley, the main route from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brenner-pass">Brenner Pass</a> into the Po plain. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-the-deacon">Paul the Deacon</a> names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euin-of-trent">Euin</a> as its first duke, who repelled Frankish invasions in the 570s and 580s and married a Bavarian princess.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a> were military lords on a sensitive frontier, dealing by war and marriage with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavarians">Bavarians</a> to the north. Their territory covered much of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trentino">Trentino</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adige">Adige</a>. Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alahis">Alahis</a> rebelled against King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunipert">Cunipert</a>, seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-pavia">Pavia</a> and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-coronate">battle of Coronate</a> around 689. Otherwise little is recorded of their government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne's</a> conquest of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard Kingdom</a> in 774, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a> was placed under Frankish counts as part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/carolingian-kingdom-of-italy">Carolingian Kingdom of Italy</a>. In 1027 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Conrad II</a> gave the county to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Trent, founding the prince-bishopric.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-trent.jpg" alt="Duchy of Trent" width="320" height="265"><figcaption>Image: Wario2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lombard_(Kingdom_of)_Italy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>569 CE – 774 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Trento</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Euin, Alahis</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombardic, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lombard Duchy of Trento</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=672&amp;focus=duchy-of-trent" aria-label="Duchy of Trent on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4943 556 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Trent lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5263 812L5218 839M5263 812L5139 672"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 839h0M5139 672h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5263 812h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5263 812h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Trento. <a href="/atlas?year=672&amp;focus=duchy-of-trent">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

